{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthConstructor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthConstructor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthFKV","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthConstructor.stripGrowth_of_periodic_fkvBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthConstructor.stripGrowth_of_periodic_fkvBound","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevStripGrowthConstructor.lean#L52-L82","doc":"**`FaddeevPhiStripGrowth` from the FKV eq-22 compact bound + same-divisor.**\nGiven\n* `hper` — the ratio `Φ/phiBProd` is periodic under both vectors of an `ℝ`-basis\n  `bas` of `ℂ` (the shift-prefactor cancellation; on main\n  `CyclicDilogPentagon.ratio_ib_periodic` / `ratio_ibinv_periodic`),\n* `hballU`, `hballL` — the two-sided FKV eq-22 ratio bound on the closed\n  fundamental ball (`‖Φ/phiBProd‖ ≤ C` and `1/C ≤ ‖Φ/phiBProd‖`),\n* `hDiv` — the same-divisor input in the direction that matters here: `Φ`\n  vanishes wherever `phiBProd b` does,\n\nthe class `FaddeevPhiStripGrowth b Φ` holds. Off `phiBProd`'s zeros the bound is\n`FaddeevStripGrowthFKV.comparable_shape_of_periodic_ballBound` (via the #4424 box\nreduction); at a zero `z` both sides collapse to `0` using `hDiv`. This *derives*\nthe previously-opaque strip-growth axiom from three literature-pinned inputs. ","signatureChunk":0}]}